      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(gateway): reject non-object MCP app tool arguments",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where users interacting with an MCP App widget could send non-object tool arguments through the Control UI bridge when a widget calls a tool. Arrays, `null`, strings, or numbers could be forwarded through `mcp.app.callTool` toward tool execution even though sibling MCP entry points already reject non-object `arguments`.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe Control UI MCP App bridge now validates optional tool `arguments` at the server-method boundary before building the `tools/call` operation. Omitted arguments still normalize to `{}`, plain objects continue through unchanged, and arrays, `null`, strings, and numbers fail before `runtime.callTool()` is reached.\n\nThe change is intentionally limited to the Control UI `mcp.app.callTool` bridge. HTTP MCP, node-host invocation, standalone MCP App parsing, tool listing, message handling, and valid object-argument tool calls are unchanged.\n\n## User Impact\n\nMCP App widget tool calls now follow the same object-only argument contract as the other MCP tool-call entry points. Malformed widget-supplied arguments fail predictably before app tool execution, while valid widget calls continue to work as before.\n\n## Evidence\n\nAI-assisted: yes.\n\nUser-realistic call chain for the affected path:\n\n```text\nMCP App iframe/widget\n  -> ui/src/components/mcp-app-view.ts:268-272 bridge.oncalltool forwards params.arguments\n  -> src/gateway/server-methods/mcp-app.ts:106-115 handles mcp.app.callTool\n  -> src/gateway/mcp-app-operations.ts:141-145 executes runtime.callTool(..., operation.params.arguments ?? {})\n```\n\nBefore this fix, the Control UI handler cast `params.arguments ?? {}` to `Record<string, unknown>` without a runtime shape check. After this fix, the handler accepts omitted/plain-object arguments and rejects invalid values before constructing the tool-call operation.\n\nFocused gateway-bridge proof added on the final head:\n\n```text\nsrc/gateway/server-methods/mcp-app.test.ts\n  does not replace a completed bridge response with a cleanup error\n    payload: arguments = { city: \"Paris\" }\n    expected response: success, content text = \"shared\"\n    execution proof: runtime.callTool(\"demo\", \"shared\", { city: \"Paris\" })\n\n  rejects non-object tool arguments before executing app tools\n    invalid arguments covered: [], null, \"city=Paris\", 42\n    expected result: \"tool arguments must be an object\"\n    execution guard: runtime.callTool is not called\n```\n\nLocal after-fix test output:\n\n```text\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/gateway/server-methods/mcp-app.test.ts --reporter=verbose\n  ✓ MCP App gateway bridge > does not replace a completed bridge response with a cleanup error\n  ✓ MCP App gateway bridge > rejects non-object tool arguments before executing app tools\n  Test Files 1 passed (1)\n  Tests 11 passed (11)\n```\n\nSibling surfaces checked:\n\n```text\nsrc/gateway/mcp-http.handlers.ts:100-105 already rejects non-object tools/call arguments.\nsrc/node-host/invoke.ts:853-854 already rejects non-object arguments.\nThe standalone MCP App path is already parsed through the MCP operation schema before execution.\n```\n\nValidation run against the final rebased head:\n\n```text\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/gateway/server-methods/mcp-app.test.ts --reporter=verbose\n  Test Files 1 passed (1), Tests 11 passed (11)\n\nnpx oxlint src/gateway/server-methods/mcp-app.ts src/gateway/server-methods/mcp-app.test.ts\n  passed\n\nnpx oxfmt --check src/gateway/server-methods/mcp-app.ts src/gateway/server-methods/mcp-app.test.ts\n  All matched files use the correct format.\n\ngit diff --check upstream/main...HEAD\n  passed\n\nnode scripts/run-tsgo.mjs -p test/tsconfig/tsconfig.core.test.json --incremental --tsBuildInfoFile .artifacts/tsgo-cache/core-test.tsbuildinfo\n  passed\n```",
        "branch": "fix/mcp-app-calltool-arguments",
